### Hardened automation gates

```bash
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py intake --zip <task.zip>
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py prepare
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py audit
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py set-verdicts --public-analysis ... --internal-validity ... --duplicate-analysis ... --reason ...
# Fixable corrections only in working_copy/
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py sync-problem-statement   # when needed
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py record-validation --check docker_build --status passed --evidence <log>
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py preflight
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py package-fixable   # or package-invalid
python automation/sentinel_submitter.py status
```

- Public/Duplicate mismatch blocks finalization and packaging.
- Multiple task roots require explicit `select-task` (no silent choice).
- Fixable packaging requires `ready_to_package` after full preflight; failed preflight creates no ZIP.
- Valid-as-is never creates a task ZIP; Invalid never creates a corrected-valid ZIP.
- Structural checks do not prove semantic correctness.
- In Fixable corrected current packages: ensure Harbor network blocks (`[environment]=public`, `[agent]=allowlist` + `allowed_hosts=["api.portkey.ai"]`, `[verifier]=no-network`); strip compose `network_mode="none"` if present; normalize `solution.patch` → `golden.patch` in working_copy only.
- New f2p tests may be added via `tests.patch` in working_copy; never edit existing p2p tests.
- Recurring traps / prompts / templates: `.cursor/rules/Sentinel_Submitter_Operational_Patterns.mdc`, `Prompts/`, `templates/`.
- Fixable packaging helpers (no verdicts): `ensure-packaging-hygiene`, `local_oracle_nop.py`.
- `tests.patch` for corrected packages must pass **`git apply --check`** (patch-only success is insufficient when renames exist).

